  {
   "title": "dc4ever, C#, 2002-2005",
   "lanes": [
    "dc4ever"
   ],
   "text": "The second Dreamcast emulator by drk||Raziel (said \"D R K Raziel\"), written in C#. Its git history is a 2019 reconstruction from backups (one commit per file at its file mtime), so its frames are approximate; the real work is 2003-2005. nullDC was partly derived from it in concept, yet the 2005 line \"{//ToDo : Check This [26/4/05]\" still lives in nullDC 3.",
   "bookmarks": [
    "sh4_opcodes 2005 line (dc4ever)",
    "dc4ever powervr.cs"
   ],
   "frames": {
    "dc4ever": [
     0,
     12
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "nullDC, 2005-2013",
   "lanes": [
    "nullDC"
   ],
   "text": "nullDC was developed closed-source from 2005; the source went public on Google Code in 2010-05 (nullDC 1.0.x). The plugin architecture (drkPvr, nullAICA, ImgReader) and the rec_v1 SH4 recompiler are here.",
   "bookmarks": [
    "nullDC rec_v1 driver",
    "nullDC drkPvr d3dRend",
    "spg.cpp (Time to emulate that stuff correctly)"
   ],
   "frames": {
    "nullDC": [
     15,
     183
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "nullDCe, the late-2008 fork",
   "lanes": [
    "nullDCe"
   ],
   "text": "nullDCe forked from nullDC mainline in late 2008 for PSP / Wii / PS3 (and later PS2). The repo is a 2017 commit of a recovered archive; the latest in-source date is 2009-10, so its first frame is dated 2009-10 (range 2008-2010). Lines present in both nullDCe 2009 and nullDC are coloured as nullDC-pre2008.",
   "bookmarks": [
    "nullDCe rec_v2 driver",
    "nullDCe rec_v2 shil",
    "nullDCe drkPvr glesRend"
   ],
   "frames": {
