  {
   "title": "HarissaDC, Xbox 360, 2026",
   "lanes": [
    "HarissaDC"
   ],
   "text": "A Dreamcast emulator for the Xbox 360 whose credits say it studied nullDC4Wii, nulldc-360 and flycast but did not copy them. The measurements agree: no own file is identical to any lane, and at most 0.5 % of its lines appear in any one lane (under 1 % in all of them together), the same level as unrelated repos. Its source arrives in one dump on 2026-11-03 (v0.2.0).",
   "bookmarks": [
    "HarissaDC SH4 PowerPC JIT"
   ],
   "frames": {
    "HarissaDC": [
     373,
     382
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "fpgadc: the hardware re-creation",
   "lanes": [
    "minicast",
    "polly2",
    "polly2-r8",
    "devtools",
    "dreamcast-tests",
    "shrike4",
    "caique",
    "wren7"
   ],
   "text": "The FPGA branch of the lineage. Every DreamSTer release pins a polly2-rtl commit (PowerVR2 in SystemVerilog) and a minicast commit (the nullDC-3-derived ARM side); each pin is a release frame: r1, r2, r2b and r3 on 2026-07-17, r4 = r5 on 2026-07-18 (r5 repins nothing), r6 on 2026-07-30 and r6b on 2026-10-24. polly2-rtl r8/develop is its own lane: the new bit-exact model has its own root commit (no merge-base with main) and carries verbatim refsw3 C++ in tb/ ref_copies*.h. shrike4 (SH4), caique (AICA), wren7 (ARM7), dreamcast-tests and dreamcast-devtools are new code.",
   "bookmarks": [
    "polly2 r6b peel_core",
    "polly2 r8 ref_copies.h (refsw3 C++ copy)",
    "shrike4 v1_core",
    "caique aica_core",
    "wren7 core"
   ],
